# Data Layer Rules

## Dexie Schema
The database is defined in src/lib/db.ts using Dexie.js 4.4.x. The schema is the source of truth.

All tables use UUIDs (crypto.randomUUID()) as primary keys. All timestamps are ISO 8601 strings. Relationships are explicit foreign keys (songId, sectionId, albumId, ideaId).

## Core Tables
- ideas — the atomic creative unit. songId=null means it's in the Idea Pool. Has optional instrumentId FK to instruments table.
- ideaMedia — audio, midi, image, file blobs attached to ideas. ZERO OR ONE of each IdeaMedia.source per idea: audio-recording, audio-import, midi-recording, step-input, midi-extraction, midi-import. Images and files unlimited (source null). Note sequences from step input are stored as IdeaMedia type midi with source step-input and notes in noteData. There is NO separate IdeaNoteSequence table.
- songs — song workspace metadata. No albumId — songs connect to albums via albumSongs junction.
- songSections — user-defined sections within a song (Verse 1, Chorus, etc.) No section-level lyrics.
- songJournalEntries — production journal entries (plain text, NOT HTML), each with an optional topic.
- songReferences — reference tracks/links/notes/attachments for a song. Each can have any combination of text + url + audioBlob + attachmentBlob.
- songAssets — artwork and file attachments at the song level.
- songTodos — checklist items per song, with optional timestamp (seconds), completion state, and sort order.
- songVersions — audio files of the actual song (rough mixes, masters, demos). One per song is marked isMain.
- albums — optional album grouping. globalNotes and referenceMaterial are plain text, NOT HTML.
- albumSongs — junction table for many-to-many album-song relationship. Songs can appear on multiple albums. Track ordering via trackNumber.
- instruments — user's saved instrument list. Name + type. No InstrumentPatch table — patch names are a plain text field (patchName) on the Idea.

## Schema Rules
- Blobs (audio, images, MIDI files) are stored in ideaMedia.blob, songAssets.blob, songReferences.audioBlob, and albums.artworkBlob.
- MIDI recordings store BOTH the .mid file blob AND parsed NoteEvent[] in noteData for fast display without re-parsing.
- NoteEvent shape: { pitch: number (0-127), startTime: number (seconds), duration: number (seconds), velocity: number (0-127) }
- sortOrder fields are integers for drag-and-drop reordering. When reordering, update sortOrder on affected items.
- patchSettings on Idea is Record<string, string> — flat key-value pairs, not nested.

## CRUD Hooks
- useDb.ts (or split into useIdeas.ts, useSongs.ts, etc.) wraps all Dexie operations.
- Every database operation must be in try/catch.
- Return the created/updated record after write operations.
- Use Dexie's liveQuery() for reactive queries that auto-update UI when data changes.
- Bulk operations (moving multiple ideas, reordering) should use Dexie transactions: db.transaction('rw', db.ideas, async () => { ... })

## When Creating New Tables or Fields
- Always add the field to the TypeScript interface in /types/ first.
- Then update the Dexie schema in db.ts.
- Increment the Dexie version number when changing indexed fields.
- Non-indexed fields can be added without a version bump.

## Future-Proofing
- No auto-increment IDs. UUIDs only.
- No Date objects. ISO 8601 strings only.
- No nested objects for relational data. Use separate tables with foreign keys.
- This schema will map 1:1 to Postgres tables when a backend is added.
